<urn:anqr:delivery-requirement-set:1> <urn:anqr:predicate:explicitlyNotRequired> <urn:usf:delivery-contract:compliancereportsaccessreviewsevidencepacks> <urn:anqr:graph:delivery-posture> .
<urn:usf:delivery-contract:compliancereportsaccessreviewsevidencepacks> <urn:usf:predicate:notRequiredReason> "There is no access to review, because there are no accounts, no roles and no personal data. The audit record the product does keep is about machine requests to one surface and is modelled as its own capability." <urn:anqr:graph:delivery-posture> .
<urn:anqr:delivery-requirement-set:1> <urn:anqr:predicate:explicitlyNotRequired> <urn:usf:delivery-contract:apikeyspersonalaccesstokens> <urn:anqr:graph:delivery-posture> .
<urn:usf:delivery-contract:apikeyspersonalaccesstokens> <urn:usf:predicate:notRequiredReason> "The agent surface verifies one operator-provisioned credential; there are no per-user keys to issue or rotate." <urn:anqr:graph:delivery-posture> .
<urn:anqr:delivery-requirement-set:1> <urn:anqr:predicate:explicitlyNotRequired> <urn:usf:delivery-contract:historyreadmodelreadonlyprojection> <urn:anqr:graph:delivery-posture> .
<urn:usf:delivery-contract:historyreadmodelreadonlyprojection> <urn:usf:predicate:notRequiredReason> "Nothing is written, so nothing has a history to project. The only server-side state is a regenerable cache whose past values carry no meaning." <urn:anqr:graph:delivery-posture> .
<urn:anqr:delivery-requirement-set:1> <urn:anqr:predicate:explicitlyNotRequired> <urn:usf:delivery-contract:enduserprofileandpreferencesselfservice> <urn:anqr:graph:delivery-posture> .
<urn:usf:delivery-contract:enduserprofileandpreferencesselfservice> <urn:usf:predicate:notRequiredReason> "Preferences are device-local, because there is no profile to hold them." <urn:anqr:graph:delivery-posture> .
<urn:anqr:delivery-requirement-set:1> <urn:anqr:predicate:explicitlyNotRequired> <urn:usf:delivery-contract:brandingandtheming> <urn:anqr:graph:delivery-posture> .
<urn:usf:delivery-contract:brandingandtheming> <urn:usf:predicate:notRequiredReason> "The product has one identity. A user brands their artefact, not the application." <urn:anqr:graph:delivery-posture> .
<urn:anqr:delivery-requirement-set:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "Twenty-four requirements and thirty-five explicit non-requirements. One candidate requirement was withdrawn during reconciliation because a separate TLS contract duplicated the existing custom-domains contract, which already owns the name, the zone and the certificate together. The remaining contracts are foundation-internal concerns with no product-facing obligation." <urn:anqr:graph:delivery-posture> .
<urn:anqr:delivery-requirement-set:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "A stated non-requirement is a commitment, not a gap. If the product later grows accounts, the honest route is a new revision that moves the contract from one list to the other, not a quiet reinterpretation of this one." <urn:anqr:graph:delivery-posture> .
<urn:anqr:delivery-requirement-set:1> <urn:anqr:predicate:bindsProfileRevision> <urn:anqr:profile-revision:3> <urn:anqr:graph:delivery-posture> .
