<urn:anqr:parity-disposition:localeparity> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:SemanticRequirement> <urn:anqr:graph:delivery-posture> .
<urn:anqr:parity-disposition:localeparity> <urn:usf:predicate:canonicalName> "localeparity" <urn:anqr:graph:delivery-posture> .
<urn:anqr:parity-disposition:localeparity> <urn:usf:predicate:objective> "Localisation is a current product commitment, not an aspiration, and locale parity is therefore a production requirement rather than a permanently undecidable facet." <urn:anqr:graph:delivery-posture> .
<urn:anqr:parity-disposition:localeparity> <urn:usf:predicate:objectiveEvidence> "Reconciliation against the legacy application: the declared denominator of 86 locales matches the legacy language table exactly, including the same seven right-to-left locales, and 86 locale resource files exist carrying exactly 1676 keys each. The two additional files in that directory are a template and a translation-tooling file, not locales." <urn:anqr:graph:delivery-posture> .
<urn:anqr:parity-disposition:localeparity> <urn:anqr:predicate:bindingStatus> "required-unrealised" <urn:anqr:graph:delivery-posture> .
<urn:anqr:parity-disposition:localeparity> <urn:anqr:predicate:unresolvedDecision> "The 86 locale resources exist as legacy evidence and are not in the product repository. Bringing them across is a delivery task with a known denominator, not a research question." <urn:anqr:graph:delivery-posture> .
<urn:anqr:parity-disposition:localeparity> <urn:anqr:predicate:unresolvedDecision> "A parity check must compare each locale against the reference locale by key set, not by file presence. Eighty-six files of the right size prove nothing about coverage." <urn:anqr:graph:delivery-posture> .
<urn:anqr:parity-disposition:localeparity> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "This disposition does not make the facet satisfied. It changes it from undecidable to required-and-unrealised, which is a different and more honest state: the subject exists, the denominator is verified, and the work is named." <urn:anqr:graph:delivery-posture> .
<urn:anqr:parity-disposition:localeparity> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "Generating translations to satisfy a count would be worse than the gap. The resources under discussion are existing human translations, and parity means agreeing with them." <urn:anqr:graph:delivery-posture> .
<urn:anqr:parity-disposition:localeparity> <urn:anqr:predicate:bindsProfileRevision> <urn:anqr:profile-revision:3> <urn:anqr:graph:delivery-posture> .
<urn:anqr:parity-disposition:surfaceparity> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:SemanticRequirement> <urn:anqr:graph:delivery-posture> .
<urn:anqr:parity-disposition:surfaceparity> <urn:usf:predicate:canonicalName> "surfaceparity" <urn:anqr:graph:delivery-posture> .
<urn:anqr:parity-disposition:surfaceparity> <urn:usf:predicate:objective> "Surface parity is a production requirement, because the product denominator commits to more than one surface. It is not yet decidable, because only one is realised." <urn:anqr:graph:delivery-posture> .
<urn:anqr:parity-disposition:surfaceparity> <urn:usf:predicate:objectiveEvidence> "Revision 3 declares responsive web delivery, mobile application delivery, HTTP API delivery and MCP delivery, and platform parity is declared cross-cutting over every action that produces or renders an artefact. The legacy tree carries platform shells for two mobile targets alongside the web application." <urn:anqr:graph:delivery-posture> .
<urn:anqr:parity-disposition:surfaceparity> <urn:anqr:predicate:bindingStatus> "required-unrealised" <urn:anqr:graph:delivery-posture> .
<urn:anqr:parity-disposition:surfaceparity> <urn:anqr:predicate:unresolvedDecision> "Exactly one surface is realised. Parity needs a second comparable subject, and which surface that is is a product sequencing decision rather than a technical one." <urn:anqr:graph:delivery-posture> .
<urn:anqr:parity-disposition:surfaceparity> <urn:anqr:predicate:unresolvedDecision> "A parity check must compare produced artefact bytes for one specification across surfaces. Comparing screenshots would test rendering, not parity." <urn:anqr:graph:delivery-posture> .
<urn:anqr:parity-disposition:surfaceparity> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "A second cosmetic surface would satisfy the count and prove nothing. The facet stays undecidable until a second surface exists because it genuinely produces artefacts." <urn:anqr:graph:delivery-posture> .
<urn:anqr:parity-disposition:surfaceparity> <urn:anqr:predicate:bindsProfileRevision> <urn:anqr:profile-revision:3> <urn:anqr:graph:delivery-posture> .
